*Rapid scaling of inference-at-deployment would somewhat lower the
importance of open-weight models (and of securing the weights of closed
models), reduce the impact of the first human-level models, change the
business model for frontier AI, reduce the need for power-intensive data
centres, and potentially undermine AI governance measures that rely on
training-compute thresholds.*

